^ 2013 - 2020`<br>`{=html}
Direct-attached storage ([DAS][]) and cold storage \
Physical(left) and logical(right). Drives lost to redundancy are displayed in
red.

 [DAS]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Direct-attached_storage

Not quite a server, but it was my first foray into this sort of thing. I got
this setup to expand the storage on my old laptop (which I had replaced with
a larger drive prior), as well as back up family media scattered across various
devices(VHS, DVD, Video8, etc.). The dual bay design seemed perfect at the time,
as it allowed me to mirror my drives for some redundancy. Eventually I ended up
with a few more drives, and needed a way to access more at a time.

|             | Hardware                  |
| ----------- | ------------------------- |
| *Chassis*   | DAS (ICY DOCK MB662U3-2S) |
| *Storage*   | 6x HDD                    |

## Ubuntu

