### Backup Server

The previous Silverstone server. I like the idea of a backup server over cold
storage, as it allows for live error detection/correction, as well as automated
backups. The OS was changed to TrueNAS, that way I could use ZFS to pull
[snapshots][] from the main server to this server. The idea is that it's faster
(because it's incremental), and better for security, as the main server (which
is more likely to be breached or infected) can't access the backup. Ubuntu can
use ZFS filesystems too, but TrueNAS is nicer for managing them.

[snapshots]: https://www.truenas.com/docs/core/13.0/coretutorials/storage/snapshots/

